Z||000000||MEC91Firebird||05-29-2001||02:44 AM||||I had the best trip this weekend!  Took a little road trip with my Dad up to the Indy 500, what a Race!  I have been wanting to go since 92 when little Al and Goodyear made a run for the finsh like .03 seconds apart.  It was really something!  Nothing like whatching it on TV, but 100x as cool.  We got to the track the afternoon before the race, and saw the Hall of fame and drove all over the infield around the track took a ride around the oval in one of the busses, and saw One Fiero at the trackm It was back behind a stand, an 84 Fiero pace car replica owned by a worker at the track.  (and I saw the model in the Hall of fame, it was cool)  Anyway, that rocked, but the next morning we drove to the track and got there at like 7 AM, there was very few people around, lots to see.  We went across the track at the end of the pits, right at turn one, an got to take pictures standing in the corner and on the front straight.  We didnt have a pit pass or anything, but we stood on a balconey that overlokked gasoline alley, right above the AJ Foyt garage.  Saw AJ Foyt, Roger Pensky, Eliso Salizar (sp?) and some others.  Anyway, We had good seats that where right at the entrance to pit lane on the outside of the track (got them for 9 under cost off ebay:-))  You could see turn 4 good, and had a great view of the cars as they went into the pits and part of the way down the main straight.  We actually where right infront of Sam Hornish when his car stop after he spun and wrecked little Al.  The safty crew was something to watch in action.  Well, I enjoyed the race, even though Andretti didnt win and both the other drivers i liked (goodyear, and little Al) got knocked out fairly early.  Well once the race ended, we went up to the start finish line to see the winners circle, and After Castronevess did his victory lap in the Bravada, he climbed the fence right infront of us.  We decided to hang around the speedway for a while and not worry about fighting traffic.  Went and saw the GM Experince display, that was pretty cool, I nearly DIED when a saw a 1989 Turbo Trans Am Pace Car, (hey, i love my fiero, but i LOVE my Firebird!!!) It was an actual Pace Car, full coplement of belts and strobe lights.  Also saw the Olds Aerotech, and the other olds pace cars.  After that we headed back to the Garage area, and kinda snuck in And wandered around.  We ran into Buddy Lazier and Eddie Chever, and then went over to the firestone Garage where Castronevis was being intervied, We didnt get to close to him, only like 15 ft away, huge crowd, but all the race tires from the cars where stacked up outside the garage, they are really something, kinda sticks to your fingers, But My brush with fame, Roger pensky  walk right next to me and my dad, and as we where leaving Castronevises Father walk by me, and I congragulated him, he shook my hand and said thanks, Really Cool!!!!  On the way home from Indy, stoped at the corvette musume in Bowling Green, Had some really Great one of a kind cars there, inclding a C4 PPG Indy racing league pace car (i think) that was done up in a fire-orange metalic paint, and had the rear end of a corvette indy, killer car.   This was just my experince, figured id share it with everyone!||||reg||6
Z||000001||FieroJoe||05-29-2001||07:33 AM||||Damn, that sounds like it was a lot of fun!  I didnt get to see much of the race on tv though, I only watched 30 min of it on my lunch break at work.  Work on sundays sucks, I always miss the races I want to watch.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/joesig_1.jpg"> <BR>'87 Coupe 5spd.<BR>AIM:FieroJoe87||||reg||1
